flowchart TB
    accTitle: Input descriptions, opened owners, and runtime delivery
    accDescr: InputPipeline combines reusable source descriptions with an optional input policy. It resolves model bindings without opening resources. Ordinary opening returns an OpenedInput that composes source data and applies the policy. Reconfigurable opening retains owners in an InputPipelineSession and delivers observations, requests, and lifecycle markers to a reconfigurable runtime.

    sources["Source descriptions: InputSources"] --> resolve["Resolve model bindings"]
    model["Model inputs and optional InputConfiguration"] --> resolve
    resolve --> plan["ResolvedInput: selected sources and bindings"]
    plan --> ordinary["Open ordinary input: OpenedInput"]
    plan --> session["Open reconfigurable input: InputPipelineSession"]
    control["Selected reconfiguration source"] -.-> session
    ordinary --> data["Compose data and apply optional InputPolicy"]
    session --> items["Compose data and requests; apply optional InputPolicy"]
    data --> runtime["Ordinary runtime receives InputBatch values"]
    items --> reconf["Reconfigurable runtime receives data and control items"]
